#SKIPTEST
' Change 1663: with #define DISABLE1663 the parameter is a warning, and the assembler then stops with its own,
' readable message (build 1662's had placeholders left in it):
' Expected (build 1663): Warning: Variable name CON is used for a system bit on the current chip, then
' Error: GCASM: CON is defined twice, as 7 and as 1: a variable, parameter, label or constant has the same name as a
' register or bit on the current chip. Rename it
#define DISABLE1663
#chip 18F46J50, 48
#option explicit
Dir PORTB Out
Do
    Show(1)
Loop

Sub Show(In COn)
    PORTB = COn
End Sub
